mmit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-11-17T07:22:33Z","state_reason":null,"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/comments/1318208634","html_url":"https://github.com/vuejs/core/issues/7160#issuecomment-1318208634","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/7160","id":1318208634,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCCum185OkkR6","user":{"login":"LittleSound","id":19204772,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjA0Nzcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19204772?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound","html_url":"https://github.com/LittleSound","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-11-17T07:34:52Z","updated_at":"2022-11-17T13:02:16Z","body":"> Computed properties are lazily evaluated. So to know wether or not their value ha changed, the need to be read by some code. So effects depending on a computed property need to run in order to find out wether the return value has changed.\r\n> \r\n> details: https://dev.to/linusborg/vue-when-a-computed-property-can-be-the-wrong-tool-195j\r\n\r\n<!-- \r\n我也发现了这个，可是这并没有解释为什么开启了 `deep` 会导致 `watch` 函数无法判断值是否变更；如果它是一个对象，我能理解；可是如果变量的值在某个时候变成了 `undefined` 或者其它基本类型的值，这个时候为什么不能简单的通过 `===` 来判断它是否变更来避免这种情况呢？\r\n-->\r\nI also found this, but it doesn't explain why turning on `deep` makes the `watch` function unable to determine if the value has changed; if it's an object, I can understand, but if the value of a variable becomes `undefined` or some other basic type at some point, why can't we simply use `===` to determine if it has changed to avoid this situation?\r\n\r\nInside `watch` it might be possible to solve this problem like this：\r\n````javascript\r\nconst needCallback = options.deep && typeof newValue === 'object'\r\n ? true\r\n : oldValue !== newValue\r\n````","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/comments/1318208634/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"LittleSound","id":19204772,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjA0Nzcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19204772?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound","html_url":"https://github.com/LittleSound","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LittleSound/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":7831106616,"node_id":"REE_lADOCCum185WmCobzwAAAAHSxTQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/events/7831106616","actor":{"login":"LinusBorg","id":1444526,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ1MjY=","avatar_url":"http